[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **The library has ZERO explicit rejection paths.** Both entry points are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `void`-returning, unconditional, straight-line code. There is no value of any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m argument for which the C returns an error, sets a code, or refuses to act — it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m always prints exactly one line.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
