[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m silently does *not* check**. Those are enumerated below one row per distinct
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m condition. For each, "expected C result" is the observable behaviour (the line
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m written to stdout), which is what the Rust must reproduce byte-for-byte; the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "error" is the absence of rejection, so the differential assertion is that Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m also does not reject and emits the identical bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
