[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 0000000000001143 T driver
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 0000000000001119 T printHexCharLine
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | level | declared in header? |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `printHexCharLine(char)` | **lowest level** — does the formatting/emission itself | no (exported but undeclared) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `driver(char)` | convenience wrapper — computes `data + 1`, then calls `printHexCharLine` | yes |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `driver` is the one-shot wrapper; `printHexCharLine` is the primitive. Both are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exercised **directly** below, and the composition `driver → printHexCharLine` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exercised as a pipeline (row C14), because a wrapper-only test cannot see a bug
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in the increment and a primitive-only test cannot see a bug in the composition.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 2 — runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m $ grep -cE 'if|switch|\?|#ifdef|#if |global|static|extern [^v]' c_src/src/driver.c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 0
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **There are no runtime options, modes, flags, or global state.** The API sets
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m nothing and branches on nothing. There is no `set_*`/`init`/`config` function,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no environment variable read, no compile-time variant. Both functions are pure
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m straight-line code over their single argument.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only *state* in play is the one both implementations share: the libc
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `stdout` stream and its buffering mode. That is an environment axis rather than a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m library option, and it is included as rows C15/C16 because output ordering and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m flush timing are part of "byte-identical".
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 3 — input shapes the code special-cases
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The complete input domain of the whole library is a single `char`, i.e. **256
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m values per entry point** — small enough to enumerate exhaustively (rows C1/C2),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m which is the strongest available check. Beyond exhaustiveness, these are the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m distinct regimes the *code path* distinguishes, all of them consequences of two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m things the C does: the default argument promotion of a **signed** `char` into the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m variadic `printf`, and the `02` minimum-width flag:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | regime | boundary constant | why the code treats it differently |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | zero | `0x00` | both digits come from the `02` pad |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | one hex digit | `0x01`–`0x0F` | one digit from the value, one from the pad |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | two hex digits, positive | `0x10`–`0x7E` | pad flag inert |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `CHAR_MAX` | `0x7F` | last non-sign-extended value; for `driver` also the input that overflows the truncating store |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `CHAR_MIN` | `0x80` (`-128`) | first sign-extended value → 8 hex digits, pad flag inert |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | negative | `0x81`–`0xFE` | sign-extended to `0xFFFFFFxx` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `-1` | `0xFF` | maximal sign extension; for `driver`, the unique input yielding `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 4 — FFI argument width (byte order / representation)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The parameter is `char`, narrower than the register that carries it. An external
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m caller can present the symbol with a full-width `int`; the SysV callee reads only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the low 8 bits. Both canonical (`i8`) and non-canonical (`c_int` with nonzero
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m upper bytes) call shapes are therefore real, distinct configurations (rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C12/C13). Byte order is not an axis: there is no multi-byte value in the API.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 5 — call multiplicity
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Single call, long sequence of calls from one library, and a sequence that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m interleaves the C and Rust `.so`s on the same `stdout` (rows C14–C16). This
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m catches lazy-initialisation and caching differences a single call cannot.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m One row per meaningful combination the C treats differently. Every row is driven
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m through **both** `.so`s' exported symbols via `libloading`, with many randomized
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inputs (fixed seed `0x5EED_C0FFEE`, SplitMix64) except where the row is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exhaustive or a single named boundary. A row is checked only after it passes
