[49m[38;5;10m+      1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Phase C — error-path differential tests, one test per row of `ERRORS.md`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! The C library has **zero explicit rejection paths** (no returns, asserts,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! error codes, range checks or null checks — see `ERRORS.md` for the grep that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! establishes this). Its error surface is therefore entirely the set of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! boundaries it silently does not check: signed-`char` sign extension, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! overflowing truncating store in `driver`, the `%02x` minimum-width flag, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! arguments outside the parameter's range presented across the FFI boundary.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
